    Performance gates:
    
    - 16K: baseline 2603.5149 token/s, threshold 0.95, pass floor 2473.3392
    token/s
    - 128K: baseline 2251.5954 token/s, threshold 0.95, pass floor 2139.0156
    token/s
    - Four-run formal mean versus baseline: -0.3250% (16K), +0.4462% (128K)
    - Formal result ranges: 2559.0361–2643.9433 token/s (16K),
    2247.0898–2281.4964 token/s (128K)
    - #17795 weighted DSpark acceptance: 66.336% (16K), 36.546% (128K)
    
    All four recorded 128K formal results also pass the updated baseline of
    2251.5954 token/s at threshold 0.95. This is a recalculation of the
    existing results, not a new benchmark run.
    
    These four successful performance observations validate the current
    Nightly configuration against its throughput gates. They do not by
    themselves prove that multithreaded model loading was the unique cause
    of the earlier regressions.
    
